  "term": "ora serrata",
  "definition": "The ora serrata is an anatomical landmark in the eye described in relation to the vitreous base and the scleral insertion of the lateral rectus muscle. In this context, it is used as a positional reference for locating retinal breaks and planning scleral buckling placement.",
